      "id": "dish_recipetin_teriyaki_salmon",
      "name": "Quick Japanese Teriyaki Salmon",
      "category": "Dinner",
      "cuisine": "Japanese",
      "servings": 2,
      "prepTimeMinutes": 10,
      "imageEmoji": "🍣",
      "imageUrl": "https://www.recipetineats.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/10/Teriyaki-Salmon_3.jpg",
      "tags": ["Japanese", "Seafood", "Quick & Easy"],
      "instructions": "1. Mix soy sauce, cooking sake, mirin, and sugar in a small bowl until the sugar dissolves.\n2. Heat a little oil in a non-stick pan over medium-high heat.\n3. Place salmon fillets skin-side down and cook for 3 minutes until the skin is crispy.\n4. Flip the salmon and cook for 1 more minute. Pour the sauce mixture into the pan.\n5. Simmer for 1-2 minutes, repeatedly spooning the bubbling glaze over the salmon until it becomes sticky and coats the fish.\n6. Serve immediately over rice with steamed greens.",
